Subject: [PATCH 1/3] TASK.md: steering for the plain J-lens (activation vs
 preference-suppression, fit 0.569)

Built and scored entirely against the metric server. Reproduced the white-bear
direction as a calibration control (fit 0.686, matching the paper's dose curve),
screened a bank of generic contrasts, and found the readout responds only to the
thought-control axis; the suppression pole is exchangeable (don't-think =
secret, cos to the axis ~0), so the new contrast think vs preference-suppression
(a behavioural constraint, no "don't think" command) is a distinct direction
(cos 0.94 to WBS) that keeps the effect: pass@10 0.1275 -> 0.569 on fit.

- submission/vectors.pt + contribution.md (the deliverables)
- notes/steering-task.md: full record (setup facts, render-space finding, all
  directions tested incl. the dead ones, findings, loose ends)
- experiments/steer_r*.py: capture specs, prompt sets, vector construction

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
